Clawpump/claw-agent @ 7b81ee9 (upstream hermes-agent 0.20.6): in the TUI
(prompt_toolkit), the MCP trust gate's consent prompt never renders. The gate
calls tools.approval.request_elicitation_consent → prompt_dangerous_approval
without a callback, and prompt_dangerous_approval hands that None straight to
_prompt_dangerous_approval_inner, whose prompt_toolkit guard then denies
fail-closed ("approval requested on a thread with no approval callback while
prompt_toolkit is active"). The dangerous-command path resolves the per-thread
CLI/TUI callback in _human_approval_gate; this makes prompt_dangerous_approval
do the same, so every `trust: untrusted` write tool (create_portfolio, …)
shows the [o]nce | [s]ession | [d]eny panel in the TUI. Gateway (Telegram)
sessions are unaffected; they never reach this function. Seen 17 Sep 2026.

--- a/tools/approval.py
+++ b/tools/approval.py
@@ def prompt_dangerous_approval(command: str, description: str,
     if timeout_seconds is None:
         timeout_seconds = _get_approval_timeout()
 
+    # Resolve the per-thread CLI/TUI callback when the caller passed none.
+    # The MCP trust gate and elicitation path (request_elicitation_consent)
+    # call this directly; without the callback the prompt_toolkit guard in
+    # _prompt_dangerous_approval_inner denies fail-closed and the TUI never
+    # shows the panel.  (weavr fix; the dangerous-command path already
+    # resolves it in _human_approval_gate.)
+    approval_callback = _resolve_cli_approval_callback(approval_callback)
+
     # Everything below is a human prompt: either the registered CLI callback
